  "name": "tsc-blindspots",
  "description": "Find type defects a green `tsc` build cannot rule out: handwritten types that disagree with an authoritative source, unchecked indexing, variance, `any` at untyped boundaries or call sites, ambient module assertions, excess-property checks, and external data asserted without validation. Substitute derived types at a fixed commit and compare `tsc` output. Audit typing edits for runtime changes: removed undefined/defaults, enum lookups, and newly optional calls. Use for JS→TS migrations, types restating existing values, rename-only refactors, or PRs claiming mechanical changes. Triggers on /mms-tsc-blindspots, \"validate this TypeScript migration\", \"is this type right\", \"does this type match the real shape\", \"why didn't CI catch this type\", \"derive vs define\", and \"what can tsc not check\". Detailed checks and examples are in the skill body and references.",
